<title>NORWAY: Nycomed 1996 net profit slumps.</title>
<headline>Nycomed 1996 net profit slumps.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31.</p>
<p>				 (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>  Operating revenue		7,738	 vs	8,388</p>
<p>Operating profit before</p>
<p>	 restructuring costs     1,335	 vs	1,914</p>
<p>  Operating profit		   535	 vs	1,914</p>
<p>Pre-tax profit before</p>
<p>	restructuring costs	1,165	 vs	1,688</p>
<p>  Pre-tax profit		     365	 vs	1,688</p>
<p>  After-tax profit		   104	 vs	1,115</p>
<p>NOTE -  Full name of Norwegian pharmaceuticals company is Nycomed ASA. Nycomed was demerged from energy group Hafslund ASA in May and listed separately on the Oslo bourse. A Reuter poll of eight analysts forecast an operating result of 595 million crowns and pre-tax profits of 427 million crowns. Two analysts recommended a buy on the share, three said hold and three said sell.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
